# Nova IT frontend environment
#
# Keep real secrets out of frontend code and out of Git.
# Public browser variables must be safe to expose.

# Optional public site URL used by future metadata or deploy checks.
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://nova-it.se

# Server-side contact form delivery. Never prefix these with VITE_ and never
# commit real values. Set the same values as Cloudflare Worker secrets.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_replace_with_a_sending_only_key
# CONTACT_FORM_FROM="Nova IT <no-reply@nova-it.se>"
# CONTACT_FORM_TO=kontakt@nova-it.se

# Secure server-to-server ticket intake into the admin portal
# (portal/app/api/public/intag/route.ts). ADMIN_INTAKE_URL is the admin
# Worker's base URL; INTAG_SECRET must match the same-named secret
# configured on the admin Worker exactly. Never prefix with VITE_.
# ADMIN_INTAKE_URL=https://admin.nova-it.se
# INTAG_SECRET=replace_with_a_long_random_shared_secret

# Cloudflare Turnstile spam protection on the contact form. The Site Key is
# public by design, but is read runtime from the Worker rather than baked into
# the Vite build. TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY is preferred; the legacy
# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY name is also supported during migration.
# TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=replace_with_your_turnstile_site_key
# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=replace_with_your_turnstile_site_key
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY is server-only and must never reach client code.
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=replace_with_your_turnstile_secret_key

# Locks the public ticket intake without taking the site down. The whole site,
# including the local support assistant, keeps working; only the submission is
# refused, and the contact page points visitors to e-mail instead. Intended for
# the window before the external penetration test and legal review are done.
#
# Server-only and never prefixed with VITE_ - it must not be settable from the
# browser. Any value other than "stangd" (including a missing or misspelled
# one) means the intake stays OPEN, so it can never silently disable itself.
# The binding check runs server-side in skickaKontaktforfragan().
# PUBLIK_INTAG_LAGE=stangd

# Cloudflare Workers AI for the support assistant's understanding layer.
# OFF by default: only the exact value "pa" enables it, so the code can ship
# to production without being active. The rule engine in support-engine.ts
# always runs first and is used whenever AI is off, misconfigured, slow or
# returns anything invalid - AI can only ever improve routing, never break it.
#
# In production this uses the native `env.AI` binding declared in
# vite.config.ts (nitro's cloudflare.wrangler.ai option) - NO secret needed
# for that path; Cloudflare authenticates the Worker to Workers AI itself.
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID/CLOUDFLARE_AI_TOKEN below are only a REST fallback
# for local `vite dev`, where no Cloudflare runtime (and so no binding)
# exists. CLOUDFLARE_AI_TOKEN, if set, must be a scoped API token with ONLY
# the "Workers AI: Read" permission. Never reuse a global API key, and never
# prefix any of these with VITE_ - they are server-only.
#
# COST: 10,000 Neurons/day are free; one classification costs a few Neurons.
# The endpoint is public and unauthenticated, so put a Cloudflare Rate
# Limiting rule in front of it before enabling. See
# docs/supportassistent-ai-drift.md.
# SUPPORT_AI_LAGE=pa
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=replace_with_your_cloudflare_account_id
# CLOUDFLARE_AI_TOKEN=replace_with_a_workers_ai_read_scoped_token
# Optional model override; defaults to @cf/meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct
# SUPPORT_AI_MODELL=@cf/meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct

# The free, multi-turn support chat ("Ärendeguiden" redesign) - a SEPARATE
# flag from SUPPORT_AI_LAGE above, so the two can be enabled independently
# during rollout. OFF by default, same "only the exact value 'pa'" rule.
# When off (or on first-turn failure), the UI falls back to the old
# rule-based guide (SupportGuide.tsx) - see SupportChat.tsx. Uses the same
# Cloudflare Workers AI binding/REST-fallback path as SUPPORT_AI_LAGE, and
# the same CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID/CLOUDFLARE_AI_TOKEN REST fallback above.
#
# COST: a chat turn (system prompt + retrieved knowledge + resent history)
# costs meaningfully more than the old single classification call, so it
# reserves the shared daily AI budget with a higher weight (see
# CHAT_BUDGET_VIKT in support-chat-server.ts and the `vikt` parameter in
# Nova-IT-Portaler/ai-budget). The endpoint is public and unauthenticated,
# and a free multi-turn chat has a much larger abuse surface than a single
# classification call - a Cloudflare Rate Limiting rule in front of it is a
# HARD prerequisite before enabling this in production, more so than for
# SUPPORT_AI_LAGE. See docs/supportassistent-ai-drift.md.
#
# Switching the model to an external vendor (e.g. Anthropic Claude) requires
# a signed-off Data Processing Agreement first - see the note at the top of
# docs/supportassistent-ai-drift.md. Do not point this at a non-Cloudflare
# provider without that sign-off.
# SUPPORT_CHAT_LAGE=pa
# Optional model override; defaults to @cf/meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct-fp8-fast
# SUPPORT_CHAT_MODELL=@cf/meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct-fp8-fast
